ll My Places\n\nDescription:\nThis illustrated children\'s book explores identity, belonging, and cultural heritage through the voice of a young boy who grows up across continents, languages, and traditions. The narrator has three different names-Lithuanian, Greek, and English-because his life is shaped by multiple places: Lithuania, Greece, the United States, Nigeria, and Ghana. Rather than presenting identity as something singular or fixed, the story affirms that children who belong to more than one culture are whole, complete, and richly connected. Through simple, personal moments-speaking different languages with each parent, attending schools on different continents, cooking foods from different heritages, and remembering life in two African countries-the book introduces young readers to multilingualism, migration, and family history in an accessible and emotionally grounded way. The narrator addresses questions many multicultural children face: Where are you "really" from? Are you only "half" of an identity? The story affirms that children with multiple heritages are not half of anything-they are completely, entirely whole. With warmth and clarity, the story challenges the idea that identity must be proven by birthplace, residence, or official documents. Instead, it emphasizes that culture can be carried through language, traditions, stories, and love. Questions that reduce or simplify identity are acknowledged with honesty, while the overall message remains affirming and hopeful. The book reframes multicultural identity as a strength, presenting children with multiple backgrounds not as divided, but as bridges between cultures. Written for children and families, it is especially resonant for third-culture kids, diaspora and immigrant communities, and multilingual households. The story concludes by inviting every reader to reflect on their own sense of belonging and affirms a powerful truth: identity is something each person has the right to define for themselves.\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
